# Loop health

Loop health shows how the loop operated. Most tiles show a percentage of time.
**Loop gaps** and **Unrecorded delivery** show a count of periods.
**Requested, not done** shows a percentage of the changes that the loop asked
for. The last two tiles show the limits that your loop reported. The charts show
the data for each hour of the day.

The [Loop Analysis overview](/docs/reports/loop-analysis) tells you about the
filters, net loop correction and how to read the charts. They are the same on
all five pages.

<Screenshot id="loop-analysis-loop-health" />

| Tile | What it shows |
|------|---------------|
| **Closed loop** | Time when the loop controlled basal delivery. |
| **CGM active** | Time when your sensor sent readings. |
| **Pump active** | Time when the loop uploaded a cycle. If there are no cycles, the report uses the delivery records. |
| **Loop gaps** | Gaps of more than 15 minutes between two loop cycles. |
| **Unrecorded delivery** | Periods when the loop operated but there is no record of the pump delivery. |
| **Algorithm zero temps** | Time when the loop set basal to zero, as a percentage of the time with known delivery. Suspends and manual zero temps are separate. |
| **At max basal** | Time when the temp basals of the loop were at the highest rate that it can set. |
| **At max IOB** | Time when insulin on board was at max IOB, as a percentage of loop time with a recorded reason (AAPS, Trio, iAPS, OpenAPS). |
| **Automatic boluses a day** | The number and the size of automatic boluses. |
| **Requested, not done** | Changes that the loop asked for but did not make, for example because the pump did not reply (AAPS, Trio, iAPS, OpenAPS). |
| **Max basal rate setting of the Loop app** and **Max IOB** | The limits that your loop reported. |

## At max basal and "max basal known"

For **Loop**, a temp is at its limit when it is at your maximum basal rate
setting. For **AAPS, Trio, iAPS and OpenAPS**, the limit is a safety limit that
the algorithm calculates each time. Only the reason that the loop gives tells
when the temp was at that limit. **Max basal known** is the percentage of the temp
time of the algorithm where Nocturne can tell. **At max basal** uses only that
time.

## Unrecorded delivery

When the loop operates but there is no record of the pump delivery, the basal
for that time is not known. Loop Analysis uses your schedule only for a gap of
3 hours or less, with records on the two sides. A large quantity of unrecorded
delivery usually means that pump history does not arrive in Nocturne. It also
makes the insulin figures on the other pages less complete.

## When a tile shows "Unknown"

When the report cannot calculate a tile, the tile shows **Unknown** and the
reason:

- **No loop cycles in this range**: the loop recorded nothing.
- **The system that ran the loop does not record this**: for example, Loop does
  not record a maximum IOB.
- **Only the Loop app uploads this setting**: the maximum basal rate setting.
- **No loop cycle in this range recorded the data that this figure needs**: the
  loop operated, but it did not record the reason that the figure uses.
- **No loop cycle in this range set the temp basals that this figure needs**: no
  loop decision matched the temps.
- **All the data for this figure is in time that the filters exclude.**
- **The active profile does not record a maximum basal rate.**
- **The loop did not set a temp basal in this range.**
- **Nothing measured in this range.**

**Max IOB** shows only when the loop reports that max IOB limited a dose.

